"""
===============================================================================
Simulation-Driven Deep Learning for Resilience Forecasting in Aging Water
Distribution Networks
===============================================================================

This file contains the two core components of the modeling framework used
in this study:

  PART 1: WNTR-based Monte Carlo simulation framework
          - Stochastic pipe aging and failure injection (Andreou et al.
            hazard model)
          - Hydraulic simulation and resilience-metric computation
            (WSA, MRI, CPI)
          - Multiprocessing simulation runner with SQLite result storage

  PART 2: Deep learning surrogate model training
          - Self-attention + residual MLP architecture (ResiliencePredictor)
          - All-networks temporal holdout training (Years 0-7 train,
            Years 8-9 test)

Setup:
    pip install -r requirements.txt
    (numpy, pandas, networkx, wntr, torch, scikit-learn, matplotlib, seaborn)

Usage:
    1. Add path(s) to your own .inp network file(s) in the `network_files`
       list inside CONFIG (Part 1), then run this file to generate
       simulation results (SQLite database + exported CSV).
    2. Update `CSV_FILE` in the __main__ block (Part 2) to point to the
       exported CSV, then run again to train the surrogate model.

Note: Network input files (.inp) and simulation output data are not included
in this repository.
===============================================================================
"""


